      "text": "This script reads only the first table in the file (the \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\" block) and stops before the other sections. Missing codes (-99.99 and -999) are treated as NaN.\n\nThe factor is the long-term reversal spread: the average of the two Low-prior-return portfolios (Small and Big) minus the average of the two High-prior-return portfolios (Small and Big). Low-prior is the loser leg, so a positive value means losers beat winners. The script drops any month where one of the four portfolios is missing.\n\n```python\nimport csv\n\nINPUT = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_60_13.csv\"\nOUTPUT = \"output.csv\"\nMISSING = {-99.99, -999.0}\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(INPUT, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the start of the value-weighted monthly table\n    start = 0\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        if \"Average Value Weighted Returns\" in line and \"Monthly\" in line:\n            start = i\n            break\n\n    records = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        is_data = (\n            len(parts) >= 7\n            and len(parts[0]) == 6\n            and parts[0].isdigit()\n        )\n        if not is_data:\n            if started:\n                break  # end of the monthly value-weighted block\n            continue\n        try:\n            date = int(parts[0])\n            vals = []\n            for x in parts[1:7]:\n                v = float(x)\n                vals.append(None if v in MISSING else v)\n        except ValueError:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        started = True\n        records.append((date, vals))\n\n    out_rows = []\n    for date, v in records:\n        # Column order: SMALL LoPRIOR, ME1 PRIOR2, SMALL HiPRIOR,\n        #               BIG LoPRIOR, ME2 PRIOR2, BIG HiPRIOR\n        sm_lo, sm_hi, big_lo, big_hi = v[0], v[2], v[3], v[5]\n        if None in (sm_lo, sm_hi, big_lo, big_hi):\n            continue\n        # LT reversal: long Low prior-return (losers), short High prior-return (winners)\n        value = 0.5 * (sm_lo + big_lo) - 0.5 * (sm_hi + big_hi)\n        out_rows.append((date, value))\n\n    with open(OUTPUT, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        writer = csv.writer(f)\n        writer.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for date, value in out_rows:\n            writer.writerow([date, repr(float(value))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
